/* book Worked example: Q: Two concentric springs of spring steel carry a total load of 10 kN with a deflection of about 80 mm. Both have spring index 6 and permissible shear stress 600 MPa; G = 81 370 MPa. Find the wire and coil diameters, the load on each, the clearance and the active coils.
   1. d₁/d₂ = C/(C − 2) = 6/4 = 1.5, so P₁/P₂ = 1.5² = 2.25. P₁ = 10 000 × 2.25/3.25 = 6923 N, P₂ = 3077 N.
   2. K = 23/20 + 0.615/6 = 1.2525. Outer: d₁² = 1.2525 × 8 × 6923 × 6/(π × 600) = 220.8, d₁ = 14.9 mm; take d₁ = 15 mm, D₁ = 90 mm.
   3. Inner: d₂ = 15/1.5 = 10 mm, D₂ = 60 mm. Both springs: τ = 1.2525 × 8 × 6923 × 90/(π × 15³) = 588.8 MPa ≤ 600.
   4. Clearance: (90 − 15)/2 − (60 + 10)/2 = 37.5 − 35 = 2.5 mm = (15 − 10)/2.
   5. Outer coils: N₁ = Gd₁⁴δ/(8P₁D₁³) = 81 370 × 15⁴ × 80/(8 × 6923 × 90³) = 8.16; take 8. Inner: N₂ = 12.24; take 12, so N₁d₁ = N₂d₂ = 120 mm.
   6. Rates: k₁ = 88.3 N/mm, k₂ = 39.2 N/mm; set deflection 10 000/127.5 = 78.4 mm; loads 6923 N and 3077 N as planned.
   Answer: Outer 15 mm wire on 90 mm mean diameter with 8 active coils (6.92 kN); inner 10 mm wire on 60 mm with 12 active coils (3.08 kN); clearance 2.5 mm; deflection 78.4 mm. */
